{
  "_comment": [
    "A SYNTHETIC Overpass response, hand-built to have the shape and the messiness of",
    "a real one. Not fetched data: the coordinates are around Sydney and the tags are",
    "realistic, but nothing here is a claim about a real charging station.",
    "",
    "Its job is to exercise every branch of the tag parsing in",
    "tools/fetch_real_network.py without making a network call, because OpenStreetMap",
    "records charger power and capacity inconsistently and that inconsistency is the",
    "hard part of the ingest. Deliberately included:",
    "  - charging_station:output in kW, and in bare watts",
    "  - a semicolon-separated list of ratings (pick the largest)",
    "  - power carried only on a socket:*:output subtag",
    "  - no power tags at all (must fall back, pessimistically)",
    "  - capacity absent, to be summed from per-socket counts",
    "  - a way with a computed centre rather than a node",
    "  - repeated names, which the schema requires to be made unique",
    "  - a station with an operator but no name, and one with neither"
  ],
